-The method typically follows a two-phase approach: **Voxelization** (determining occupied voxels) and **Geometry Generation** (creating mesh primitives from those voxels). Implementations vary between CPU-based hash-table approaches (e.g., Point-Cloud-Utils, madcad) and GPU-based rasterization pipelines. The following details the CPU-based hash-table approach, which is explicitly defined in the sources [S4, S3, unofficial].
