-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Holes**: Standard rasterization may miss voxels if triangle edges fall between voxel centers. The `precision` parameter helps mitigate this, but conservative rasterization is preferred for completeness [S2, unofficial][S1].
-*   **Performance**: The output mesh size scales with voxel density. A torus with 441 input vertices can produce 61,312 output vertices at size 0.75, and 144,968 at size 0.5 [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Memory**: Using a hash table (sparse voxelization) is more memory-efficient than a dense 3D array for sparse meshes [S3, unofficial].
